{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if his means do not suffice for a sheep</b> — Scripture dealt leniently with the sinner in these matters, to allow him to bring a korban oleh veyored (a graduated offering according to means). It is possible that the reason regarding the oaths is that they are not subject to karet, and regarding the defilement of the Sanctuary and its consecrated offerings, it is because he is erring in a matter of a commandment — for the priest who eats consecrated offerings and the one who comes to the Sanctuary to bow down or to offer a korban is engaged in a commandment and his intent is toward Heaven. Therefore, even though he sinned by concealing his defilement, Scripture multiplied for him the offerings of atonement. And Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Leviticus 5:7) said that the reason for \"one for an olah\" is that it is offered on the altar in place of the emurim (the portions burned on the altar) in an animal chatat. And his explanation is fine."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:41.120340462Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}